Mae: heads-up — terraform plan for staging removed the IRSA annotation from the uploader service account. saw it in CI plan output. anyone know why? :eyes:
Mae: plan snippet:
```hcl
- resource "kubernetes_service_account" "uploader" {
-   metadata {
-     name = "uploader"
-     namespace = "staging"
-     annotations = {
-       "eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn" = "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/redwood-staging-uploader"
-     }
-   }
- }
```
Mae: didn't touch that module, just bumped version of modules/s3-uploader

raj: hmm, did we switch provider alias or move the SA out of k8s provider? saw something similar when we migrated eks cluster provider.
raj: can you share the plan link or `terraform state show`?

infra-bot: terraform plan for PR #842 — https://ci.redwood.ai/plan/842 — detected resource change: kubernetes_service_account.k8s.uploader (deletion)

evan: likely cause: new module removed `annotations` from template, so plan shows deletion. quick check: `terraform state show module.s3-uploader.kubernetes_service_account.uploader` — if state has annotation we need to add it back or import.
evan: try this patch in the module values:
```hcl
service_account_annotations = {
  "eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn" = var.uploader_role_arn
}
```

mae: running `terraform state show` now, will paste output in a sec

mae: pasted — state still has annotation entry (role arn). plan shows deletion though.

raj: maybe there's a null/empty map default swallowing it now. module defaults to `{}` and Helm/manifest logic omits annotations if map empty. check module version diff.

mae: bumping module back to previous commit in a test branch stops deletion. reopening module PR to re-add annotation passthrough.

evan: another short-term fix: add a lifecycle ignore_changes on metadata.annotations for that resource to avoid accidental removal:
```hcl
resource "kubernetes_service_account" "uploader" {
  lifecycle {
    ignore_changes = [metadata[0].annotations]
  }
}
```
evan: not ideal long-term but buys time.

mae: @raj @evan thanks — I'm going to hold the rollout and open a tiny patch. will ping when PR ready :thumbsup:

raj: :+1:
infra-bot: reaction :eyes:
